+# Neuromorphic Compiler V2 – X2 AI Tooling Flow
+![X2 AI Tooling Flow](ai_tooling_x2.PNG)
+This repo is a runnable prototype of the X1 AI tooling flow shown in your
+architecture sketch. It keeps the lane split you asked for but now also
+integrates a basic **ExecuTorch compiler/runtime**. Where the original
+prototype generated only a compile specification and delegate metadata,
+this version produces a fully serialized program in `.pte` format using
+either the optional ExecuTorch compiler or a TorchScript fallback.
+
+- **ExecuTorch lane** – generates a compile specification and delegate
+  metadata and now also compiles the model to a serialized program
+  `artifacts/executorch_program.pte`. When the `executorch` package
+  is installed the program is produced via `executorch.compile`; if
+  unavailable, a TorchScript trace is saved instead.
+- **Compiler lane** – for graph capture, validation, quantization, tiling, and mapping.
+- **MAESTRO lane** – for per-layer dataflow description generation, mapping, and scheduling.
+- **Runtime lane** – for memory planning, dispatch, and verification.
+- **Deployment lane** – for quantized deployment status and export hooks.
